WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:22.900
every day people ride buses to places near&nbsp;
and far today we are taking a long bus ride&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:30.490
here in the bus station we must first buy a ticket&nbsp;
Jorge and his father are buying their tickets now

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:43.240
they are just in time for our buses coming&nbsp;
into the station it is big and powerful

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:57.060
mr. Fisher drives our bus he has driven buses&nbsp;
for many years this man tells us when the bus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:06.990
is ready he doesn't lose the loudspeaker one&nbsp;
five seven thirty coach for Somerville Easton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:16.980
Harrisburg Bedford Pittsburgh and the West&nbsp;
time to go many people are going with us the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:24.450
porter puts away our baggage in a space under&nbsp;
the seats mr. Fisher takes George's ticket

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:39.470
inside the passengers are finding their&nbsp;
seats George likes to sit in front so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:46.280
he can watch the driver before mr. Fisher&nbsp;
starts the bus he closes the door and starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:56.750
the motors then he backs the bus away&nbsp;
out of the station we go and on our way

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.130
right on time too

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:12.710
mr. Fisher drives carefully in crowded&nbsp;
city streets watching out for cars and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:20.600
people he switches a signal the signal to warn&nbsp;
drivers behind him that he wants to make a turn

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.810
one last look at the tall buildings&nbsp;
as we leave the city behind

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:42.880
soon we are out on the open highway a&nbsp;
highway that is like a river flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:54.910
from city to city cars buses and trucks&nbsp;
roll over it day and night George likes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.910 --> 00:03:01.120
to see the big trucks like these hauling all&nbsp;
kinds of goods to the factories and stores

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:10.390
but mr. Fisher keeps his eyes on the road&nbsp;
watching the road and the other cars all the time

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:24.880
a traffic light stops us we will lose a&nbsp;
minute or two here and mr. Fisher has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:38.350
keep track of the time 9:56 he's still&nbsp;
on schedule but now the stoplight is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:48.940
changing to go he shifts gears he moves&nbsp;
ahead quickly he still has many miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:54.610
of driving to do he knows just how fast&nbsp;
to go on each part of the road to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.610 --> 00:04:00.760
on time and to drive safely now watch&nbsp;
this driver coming out of a side road

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:09.890
mr. Fisher has to look out for all&nbsp;
kinds of careless drivers on the highway

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:21.110
he sees in a big mirror cars coming&nbsp;
from behind here comes a car passed now

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:25.980
here comes another

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:34.180
mr. Fisher always drives safely and never passes&nbsp;
another car when he can't see the road ahead

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.350
now we are riding through a fine farm country

00:04:50.730 --> 00:05:02.490
look there farm boys and girls wishing the driver&nbsp;
good luck as we roll onward a train is coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:09.790
but we'd need not stop for trains our highway&nbsp;
goes under the railroad through this underpass

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:23.700
as our bus goes on the passengers are&nbsp;
having a pleasant time some watch the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:29.970
scenery others read while others find&nbsp;
napping the most pleasant way to travel

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:47.070
look ahead there's a car stalled on the&nbsp;
highway our driver puts on the brake and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:56.070
he turns out carefully the driver must&nbsp;
be ready to act quickly at last we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.070 --> 00:06:06.990
coming into another city the bus turns into a&nbsp;
station much like the one from which we started

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:19.920
here's some of the passengers&nbsp;
are leaving this this is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:27.540
end of the trip for mr. Fisher to&nbsp;
and so George tells him goodbye

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:38.040
a new driver mr. Thompson will&nbsp;
take us on from here mr. Fisher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:45.960
turns over the tickets everything&nbsp;
in order mr. Thompson is ready to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:54.390
go to work soon we are leaving the&nbsp;
city on the second part of our trip

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:06.890
we cross a broad beautiful river out on&nbsp;
the road mr. Thompson settles to his word

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:16.530
in a little while we reached the&nbsp;
entrance to a great superhighway

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:34.080
on this wide superhighway mr. Thompson can drive&nbsp;
more safely and more easily and passengers can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:42.570
ride more comfortably two cars that cross this&nbsp;
highway have to use bridges overhead like this one

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:55.440
why'd separate lanes and well-built&nbsp;
curves mean faster safer driving

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:11.430
we are nearing a mountain ridge it is a high wall&nbsp;
across our path but we plunge into this tunnel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:20.510
right through the mountain out on the other side&nbsp;
and down the mountainside into the valley beyond

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:33.000
now we come to a place where the&nbsp;
bus stops to give us a short rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:46.860
a place to stretch our legs and to eat lunch&nbsp;
a nice lunch room by the side of the highway

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:56.820
while Jorge and his father and the other&nbsp;
passengers have lunch mr. Thompson makes sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:04.710
the tires have plenty of air he looks at the big&nbsp;
motor to see that it has plenty of water and oil

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:20.570
now he can go to lunch too&nbsp;
in a little while we are on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:26.120
our way again the passengers settle&nbsp;
down for the last hours of the trip

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:38.620
mile after mile goes by as mr. Thompson drives on

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:50.910
now we cross a valley a valley of steel mills and&nbsp;
factories we're nearing the end of our long ride

00:09:55.330 --> 00:10:05.050
mr. Thompson's worked for the day is almost&nbsp;
over the passengers get ready to leave the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:13.000
bus hats and coats go on journeys and mr.&nbsp;
Thompson has driven another long bus trip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:24.340
safely and on-time tomorrow he will drive&nbsp;
back over the same Road now it's goodbye to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:32.290
mr. Thompson and goodbye to George let's hope&nbsp;
we'll take a bus trip together again very soon

